Split from the original Part A by the owner (2026-09-28). Design: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-content-keyed-panel-caches-design.md` (branch `docs/part-a-content-keyed-caches`) — the ht_server half of it.

**Why:** with Part B (panels follow the store) the user-visible stale-panel problem is solved by rebuild + restart. What remains is content that changes WITHOUT a model change — above all a developer editing a store-side generator or its Rhai: the XML changes under the same `script_path`, and ht_server keeps serving the old compile until something invalidates it. That is what `DisableServerSideCache` ("useful for debugging schema changes") and `ServerCached` exist to paper over.

**Scope:**
- compile key = `(form_factor, size, script_path, blake3(XML))`;
- every resolver answer recorded per variant (path→id, is-image, provider-ref, DisplayName adopter — errors included) and re-checked in `CompiledPanelScript::serves`;
- bounded LRU with an atomic hit tick (no write lock on a hit; never the cache lock under the proxy guard);
- debug builds recompile on every hit and log ERROR on a difference (owner Q4);
- `DebugScripts=true` forces a compile (Q5);
- remove `DisableServerSideCache` (all consumers in ONE commit — the spec's list: 29 store.toml lines, 5 template-build scripts, CLI, config known-key filter, login allowlist, tests, docs, skills; a leftover key WARNs and is ignored, Q8) and `ServerCached` / `ServerCache="false"` / `xml_declares_no_server_cache` after the content key lands; retire the staleness-only `InvalidateCache` fires (Q9).

**Owner questions for this half:** Q4, Q5, Q8, Q9, Q11 (spec §3).
**Not in scope:** the renderer (A2, deferred), `Cached` → `Lifetime` and the `*` definition-name prefix (A2).
